          A solar generator is only as good as its solar input. Most kits ship with one panel on a station that can take three, and the charge times on the box assume a perfect day. The real figure is closer to 70 percent of rated panel output across four to six hours of strong sun. Here is how to do that maths, and which kits are built to use it.
